 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-080: Exp4341 Either Reproduces sc25 L1 Or Records An Honest Win-Mechanic Partial
 **Description:** Running Exp 4341 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_sc25` when the local sc25 simulator is absent, writes `success_e3_sc25_L1_reproduced` only when the induced-model plan cracks a complete win path and independently reproduces at least L1 offline, or writes `complete_e3_sc25_partial_model_<acc>` when the bounded explore-verify-plan attempt does not reach the reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `offline_reproduced=true`, `reproduced_levels>=1`, `win_mechanic_cracked=true`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, preserve the world model path and hash, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world model hash, plan, reproduction result, verifier rounds, win-mechanic flag, and random seed. A partial run MUST set `offline_reproduced=false`, `reproduced_levels=0`, preserve `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, preserve the world model path and hash, report the best verifier accuracy and residual mismatch class, and record the residual mismatch as a missing-world-model-rule gap rather than claiming a solve.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-081: ARC-AGI-3 Frame-Only Mechanic-Class Strategy Router
+**Description:** The system SHALL provide a two-tier solving router for ARC-AGI-3 in which a STRATEGY-class decision precedes the goal-distance HEURISTIC decision, so that a game is routed to a solving strategy appropriate to its control MECHANIC before any heuristic is selected. `python/carnot/agentic/arc_strategy_router.py` MUST map a detected mechanic class to its strategy descriptor (solver entrypoint, search engine, applicability features, and whether a solver is wired), and MUST short-circuit the goal-distance heuristic portfolio for any class where it does not apply (the program-editor class, where blind clicks cannot drive multi-attribute alignment). Mechanic detection MUST follow live-correct precedence: an INJECTED frame-only verdict (the classifier `scripts/arc3_frame_induction.py:induce`, which uses ONLY `grid_of(frame)` + `levels_completed(frame)` with zero internal-state access — the unseen-live-game path) takes precedence over a structured `mechanic_class` recorded in `ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml` (a known game), which takes precedence over the `graph_explore` default. The router MUST recognise the discovered mechanic taxonomy (`program_editor`, `graph_explore`, `checkpoint_multirun`, `timed_trap_aware`) and MUST report `wired: False` for any class whose frame-only solver is not yet built rather than implying a solver exists. `arc_solve_learning.recommend_approach(game, mechanic=...)` MUST surface the routed `strategy` as its first decision and MUST replace the `heuristic_policy` with a `not_applicable`/`strategy_solver`/`needs` record for non-`graph_explore` classes. The program-editor strategy's `needs` MUST name the offline-trained transition verifier that the frame-only no-graded-feedback limit requires (cf. `ops/verifier_gaps.md` GAP-ARC-PROGRAM-EDITOR-NO-GRADED-FEEDBACK).
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-081: A Program-Editor Game Routes To Its Frame-Only Model And Skips The Heuristic Portfolio
+**Description:** Calling `route_for_game("tn36")` (or `recommend_approach("tn36")`) MUST return the `program_editor` strategy with `wired=True` and `uses_goal_distance_heuristic=False`, and `recommend_approach` MUST return a `heuristic_policy` marked `not_applicable` (carrying the strategy solver + the offline-transition-verifier `needs`) rather than the goal-distance portfolio. Calling the router for a `graph_explore` game (e.g. `r11l`) MUST keep the trained heuristic router (`heuristic_policy` containing `trained_router`). An UNSEEN game whose frame-only classifier returns `program_editor` MUST route to the program-editor strategy when that verdict is injected via `mechanic=`, with no registry or internal-state dependency. A recognised-but-unwired class (`timed_trap_aware`) MUST route with `wired=False` and a reason naming that its frame-only solver is not yet wired; an injected mechanic outside the taxonomy MUST fall back to `graph_explore`.
